v 3
d projectbackup. Zip up a project folder, subfolders included, in native Stata.
d
d projectbackup archives a folder and everything under it into a single
d .zip using only Stata's own zipfile command and Mata -- no tar, 7-Zip,
d or PowerShell, so it behaves identically on macOS, Windows, and Linux
d and works where you cannot run external programs.
d
d It is built for the everyday "snapshot my project" habit: point it at a
d folder and it writes a (optionally dated) zip into an _archive subfolder,
d and can keep a running Markdown log of every backup.  Before writing it
d walks the tree and warns about oversized folders, too many files, and
d paths too deep for Windows to extract -- with a dryrun that measures
d without writing.  Options: archive(), prefix(), timestamp, label(),
d exclude(), nodotfiles, toc, note(), manifest, keep(), removeall, dryrun,
d force, and a zippy option that also writes a Stata Journal .zippy copy.
d
d   projectbackup [folder] [, timestamp toc exclude() keep() dryrun ...]
d
d Requires: Stata 14+ (uses zipfile and Mata; nothing external).
d
d KW: backup
d KW: archive
d KW: zip
d KW: zipfile
d KW: project
d KW: reproducibility
d KW: Stata Journal
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth
